WEBVTT

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:37.746
Huh?

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.795
I choose to not understand these signs.

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.549
- A-ha.
- B... Bender.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:50.342
I was just not playing the Holophonor.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.719
Yeah? Well, you should try
not stinking at it.

00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:55.597
Well, I am trying.
I've been taking lessons.

00:00:55.681 --> 00:00:57.850
Lessons? Ha, that's rich.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:00:59.309
Isn't it time you gave up all hope

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:01.520
of ever improving yourself in any way?

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.939
I know I should, but I just can't.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.692
Remember when I had
those stomach worms that made me smart?

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:09.403
I could play the Holophonor,
and it made Leela like me.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:13.198
Hey, Bender, as long as you know,

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:15.242
I have a Holophonor recital Tuesday

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.911
and I'd really like
to have somebody there. Please?

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:20.414
Fine, I'll go already.

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:23.625
You know, sometimes I wish
your real parents were still alive.

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:26.670
Not often, though.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.632
Whoa, whoa. Whoa, whoa.

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:31.800
Hey.

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:38.223
- Uh, hello, Mrs. Mellinger.
- Hello, Philip.

00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:40.142
And you must be Mr. Bender.

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:42.519
Philip's told me so much about you.

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:44.521
Is it true that you're a robot?

00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:47.983
I prefer the term "Love machine."

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:11.048
Wow, your kid is great.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.133
How hard did you say you had to hit him?

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:14.927
Fairly hard.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.017
The Grumpy Snail.

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:30.692
Sorry.

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:43.330
It's too grumpy.

00:02:49.461 --> 00:02:50.587
Whoo!

00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:54.007
Mr. Bender, I simply
cannot teach your child.

00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:56.176
Then good day, madam.

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:03.600
We hope to see you soon for tea.

00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:06.019
It's hopeless.

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:08.188
I can hear all this great music in my head

00:03:08.272 --> 00:03:10.148
but my stupid hands can't keep up.

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:12.359
Aw, you know what always cheers me up?

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:15.529
Laughing at other
people's misfortunes.

00:03:16.405 --> 00:03:19.366
Hey, guys, you missed
a great delivery to Space Earth.

00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:20.701
Where you been all afternoon?

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:22.077
At a... A concert.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.079
Ooh, was it jazz noodling?

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:26.540
My ex-boyfriend Sean played the sax.

00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:27.916
I used to listen for hours

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.669
while he sat naked on my couch
and improvised.

00:03:30.752 --> 00:03:33.630
So, musicians really
Rodger your Hammerstein, huh?

00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:35.257
Yeah, it's weird.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.759
Sean was uneducated, unambitious,

00:03:37.843 --> 00:03:40.220
- he was pasty and hunched...
- Pretty boy.

00:03:40.304 --> 00:03:41.763
...but when he played

00:03:41.847 --> 00:03:46.185
I could sense this incredible,
beautiful, creative soul.

00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:49.938
Then one day, I found someone else's
couch fibers on his butt.

00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:52.232
I couldn't even believe that.
It was really...

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:54.151
That could be my beautiful soul

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.777
sitting naked on her couch

00:03:55.861 --> 00:03:58.280
if I could just
learn to play this stupid thing.

00:03:58.363 --> 00:03:59.740
Oh, but you can.

00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:01.491
Though you may have to metaphorically

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:02.784
"make a deal with the Devil."

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.120
And by "Devil," I mean Robot Devil,

00:04:05.204 --> 00:04:07.915
and by "Metaphorically,"
I mean get your coat.

00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:17.341
You hit a sour note

00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:19.635
about 200 years back, Doug.

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:21.094
Let's take it from the top.

00:04:22.137 --> 00:04:25.307
Ah, Bender, Fry!

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.851
You've come back
for more eternal damnation.

00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:30.062
No, this isn't a religious visit.

00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:32.105
Fry just wants Holophonor lessons.

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:34.274
Yep. I need to get
really good without practicing.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.153
Hell is full of ten-year-olds

00:04:38.237 --> 00:04:40.531
who wanted exactly the same thing.

00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:43.450
Trouble is, you have
what my old music teacher

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:46.828
Mrs. Mellinger, calls "Stupid Fingers."

00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:48.497
With hands like that

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.707
you'll be lucky to master a belt buckle.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:53.794
Now, wouldn't it be nice

00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:56.380
if you had a pair of robot hands

00:04:56.463 --> 00:04:57.714
to replace them?

00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:58.966
Sure would.

00:04:59.049 --> 00:05:00.801
Oh, well. Good-bye.

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:02.427
Fry, you smelly idiot.

00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:05.639
I think he's willing to make some kind
of a deal with the Devil with you.

00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:07.933
He... He is? Great.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:09.226
Wait, what's the catch?

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.644
No catch.

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:12.646
I'll merely pick a robot at random

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:14.481
from somewhere in the universe,

00:05:14.565 --> 00:05:15.941
probably one you've never even met,

00:05:16.024 --> 00:05:17.442
and then I'll remove his hands

00:05:17.526 --> 00:05:19.236
and switch them for yours.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.614
It's just the sort of guy I am.
What do you say?

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:24.491
Uh, I don't know.

00:05:24.575 --> 00:05:26.076
It doesn't seem entirely moral to...

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.287
Fry, if you don't take
this offer right now

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.497
I will lose all respect
for you and punch you.

00:05:32.583 --> 00:05:34.960
Well... all right.

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:36.295
You're sure I probably won't know him?

00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:37.921
Definitely probably not.

00:05:38.005 --> 00:05:40.215
- Just sign this contract...
- Wow.

00:05:42.551 --> 00:05:44.469
And here we go.

00:05:47.097 --> 00:05:49.683
I got a hundred bucks on Rectal-Exam-Bot.

00:06:05.741 --> 00:06:07.868
"Robot Devil?"

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:10.120
I get your hands? 'Zam!

00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:13.332
Oh, what an appallingly ironic outcome.

00:06:13.415 --> 00:06:15.751
It's not ironic. It's just coincidental.

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:18.378
Now fork over those ladyfingers, cookie.

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:22.633
You know, I only put my name on there

00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:25.052
as a show of good faith
for the other robots.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.888
Stop being such a baby
and chop my hands off.

00:06:27.971 --> 00:06:29.556
Oh, very well.

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:33.894
How'd you do that?

00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:36.063
They're very good hands.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:37.356
At last.

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:39.733
At last I have the power
to make Leela love me.

00:06:42.861 --> 00:06:45.072
Oh, sorry.
That'll wear off in a couple of days.

00:06:52.079 --> 00:06:54.081
Check it out, everyone. I'm back from Hell

00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:56.041
and I've got the Robot Devil's hands.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:58.168
Neat. Let's see a trick.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.004
All righty.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:06.218
Somebody called the Robot Devil's here

00:07:06.301 --> 00:07:08.178
to see somebody called Fry.

00:07:08.262 --> 00:07:09.429
Uh-oh.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.058
Where'd I go just now?

00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:16.103
Hello, Fry.

00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:19.815
Just dropped by to make sure

00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:22.401
you're as happy
with our little deal as I am.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:25.904
Oh... give me back my hands.

00:07:26.363 --> 00:07:30.075
These things are always
touching me in places.

00:07:31.618 --> 00:07:33.161
Yeah, they get around,

00:07:33.245 --> 00:07:34.830
but I'm afraid we had a deal.

00:07:34.913 --> 00:07:37.583
Looks like I wasted a bus trip.

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:39.418
Yes, you did.

00:08:13.869 --> 00:08:17.247
Yes, now you can hear
Holophonor virtuoso Philip Fry

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:20.125
play 900 of these classic themes
in your own home

00:08:20.209 --> 00:08:21.877
on this two-record set.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.047
That's over 30 minutes
of music for only $14.99.

00:08:25.547 --> 00:08:29.259
Only $14.99 for a two-record set.

00:08:29.343 --> 00:08:30.511
Two records.

00:08:30.886 --> 00:08:34.932
Oh, Zoidberg, at last you're
becoming a crafty consumer.

00:08:35.015 --> 00:08:37.309
- Hello.
- Hello? I'll take eight.

00:08:39.853 --> 00:08:41.980
A Mr. Hedonismbot to see you.

00:08:42.064 --> 00:08:44.525
- Uh, show him in.
- Very good, sir.

00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:47.819
Ah, Fry, congratulations.

00:08:47.903 --> 00:08:49.780
Your latest performance was as delectable

00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:52.157
as dipping my bottom over and over

00:08:52.241 --> 00:08:55.327
into a bath
of the silkiest oils and creams.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.453
Thank you, sir.

00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:58.247
That's exactly what I was going for.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.581
You were the sole diversion

00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:03.085
in what has been a pale
and un-amusing season,

00:09:03.168 --> 00:09:06.421
and so, I would fain commission
you write an opera.

00:09:07.339 --> 00:09:09.132
But I've never written an opera.

00:09:09.216 --> 00:09:11.051
And I've never heard one.

00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:14.304
Still, if you can keep me amused
through the overture

00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:17.182
I shall consider it a smashing success.

00:09:17.516 --> 00:09:20.561
But I wouldn't even know
what to write about. Unless...

00:09:25.983 --> 00:09:27.359
Okay, I'll do it

00:09:27.442 --> 00:09:29.319
if I can make it about Leela.

00:09:29.778 --> 00:09:31.113
Me? Really?

00:09:31.488 --> 00:09:34.449
A man writing an opera about a woman?

00:09:35.951 --> 00:09:39.162
Oh, sirrah, how deliciously absurd.

00:09:39.246 --> 00:09:40.998
I shall see you at the premiere.

00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:06.815
Is it part of the opera?

00:10:06.899 --> 00:10:08.650
Leela. You shouldn't be listening.

00:10:09.026 --> 00:10:10.819
I don't want you to hear it
till it's done.

00:10:10.903 --> 00:10:12.362
But it's so beautiful.

00:10:12.738 --> 00:10:15.365
So is a peacock,
but you don't eat it until it's cooked.

00:10:15.449 --> 00:10:16.992
This has to be perfect.

00:10:17.075 --> 00:10:19.119
I want you to hear exactly what I hear

00:10:19.203 --> 00:10:20.454
when I think about you.

00:10:20.746 --> 00:10:24.082
Oh, Fry, all this time
you've had this incredible gift

00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:25.626
and I never knew.

00:10:25.709 --> 00:10:29.338
I've been a fool,
a fully justified, prudent fool.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:33.759
They're so cold.

00:10:33.842 --> 00:10:36.053
And yet Hell is so hot.

00:10:38.597 --> 00:10:40.057
Can I have my hands back now?

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.851
- No!
- You're not nice.

00:10:49.441 --> 00:10:52.236
Ah, Bender, this is a surprise...

00:10:52.319 --> 00:10:54.947
for you, finding me in the refrigerator.

00:10:55.364 --> 00:10:57.699
True, but at least
I don't have the hiccups anymore.

00:10:57.783 --> 00:10:59.576
- What up?
- Oh, well, it so happens

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:02.037
I'm in the mood to make a deal with you.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.040
- Forget it. you can't tempt me.
- Really?

00:11:05.374 --> 00:11:07.292
There's nothing you want?

00:11:07.876 --> 00:11:10.504
Hmm. I forgot you could tempt me
with things I want.

00:11:10.838 --> 00:11:13.882
Well, I suppose I've always wondered
what it would be like

00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:16.051
to be more annoying.

00:11:16.593 --> 00:11:18.303
Nothing simpler,

00:11:18.387 --> 00:11:21.014
and all I ask in return is your hands

00:11:21.098 --> 00:11:23.809
to replace these bony hot dogs.

00:11:23.892 --> 00:11:25.519
Grabby and Squeezy?

00:11:25.602 --> 00:11:27.479
Never. I love these guys.

00:11:27.563 --> 00:11:30.482
Well, is there anything else
you would part with?

00:11:30.566 --> 00:11:32.943
No, nothing, ain't gonna happen.

00:11:34.862 --> 00:11:37.239
Yes. With this built-in stadium air horn

00:11:37.322 --> 00:11:39.157
I can really annoy people

00:11:39.241 --> 00:11:41.368
and all it cost me was my crotch plate.

00:11:42.035 --> 00:11:45.122
You certainly are
a shrewd businessman, Bender.

00:11:46.206 --> 00:11:49.084
Now find someone
and give them a good blast.

00:11:49.168 --> 00:11:51.962
Yeah, that'll teach
the first person I see a lesson.

00:11:53.172 --> 00:11:55.757
Ah, my ridiculously circuitous plan

00:11:55.841 --> 00:11:57.759
is one quarter complete.

00:12:01.471 --> 00:12:03.724
Well, Fry's opera
premieres tomorrow night.

00:12:03.807 --> 00:12:05.475
I'm off to find a pair of formal gloves

00:12:05.559 --> 00:12:07.436
that will fit over my enormous forearms.

00:12:13.567 --> 00:12:14.818
Pretty annoying, huh, Leela?

00:12:14.902 --> 00:12:17.029
What? Are you talking?

00:12:17.112 --> 00:12:18.864
Oh, God, I'm deaf.

00:12:19.239 --> 00:12:22.034
Oops. I'm so, so sorry, Leela.

00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:23.368
I just wanted to annoy you.

00:12:23.452 --> 00:12:26.288
What? Oh, this is horrible.

00:12:26.371 --> 00:12:28.665
I won't be able to hear Fry's opera.

00:12:31.084 --> 00:12:33.420
Ah, how delightfully ironic.

00:12:33.504 --> 00:12:34.880
It's not ironic.

00:12:34.963 --> 00:12:37.090
It's just mean. Take this.

00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:41.762
Ooh, out of aerosol.

00:12:41.845 --> 00:12:43.096
Also ironic.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:44.223
Oh, yeah?

00:12:44.306 --> 00:12:46.517
Well, bite my shiny metal...

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.561
Oh, no!

00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:00.906
Nobody tell Fry I'm deaf.

00:13:00.989 --> 00:13:02.866
If he found out I couldn't hear his opera,

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.076
it'd break his heart.

00:13:04.159 --> 00:13:05.410
Okay, deaf-o.

00:13:06.995 --> 00:13:09.373
Courtesans and gentlefops,

00:13:09.456 --> 00:13:12.793
I bid you welcome to my opera.

00:13:12.876 --> 00:13:15.921
Let us cavort like the Greeks of old.

00:13:16.004 --> 00:13:17.756
You know the ones I mean.

00:13:24.513 --> 00:13:26.890
Yay, Fry.

00:13:26.974 --> 00:13:28.725
I watch TV with that guy.

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:47.369
Who is this one-eyed
female baby Moses?

00:13:47.452 --> 00:13:50.497
With courage in her female baby smile?

00:13:51.164 --> 00:13:52.916
A savior from the stars

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.251
Or something stranger still?

00:13:54.334 --> 00:13:57.963
Or just a lonely, filthy, starving child?

00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:01.466
Amy, Fry's looking at me.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:03.260
What am I supposed to be feeling?

00:14:05.012 --> 00:14:06.013
Ah.

00:14:09.474 --> 00:14:11.226
Leela

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.103
Leela, Leela

00:14:13.187 --> 00:14:14.229
Save him

00:14:14.313 --> 00:14:16.273
Save Fry, save Fry

00:14:16.356 --> 00:14:19.693
Godzilla will devour him

00:14:19.776 --> 00:14:21.236
As for me, I must be off

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:24.198
To have my doctor check this cough

00:14:25.365 --> 00:14:26.575
Good-bye

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.704
I don't recall ever fighting Godzilla,

00:14:30.787 --> 00:14:32.998
but that is so what I would have done.

00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:34.791
Oh, it was a lovely show.

00:14:38.295 --> 00:14:40.380
One diet double martini, please.

00:14:40.464 --> 00:14:41.507
And for you, sir?

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.592
I'll just have a Shirley Hemphill.

00:14:43.675 --> 00:14:45.219
Extra, extra.

00:14:45.302 --> 00:14:48.472
World's greatest opera only half over.

00:14:48.555 --> 00:14:50.682
Half over? Oh!

00:14:50.766 --> 00:14:52.434
I'd give anything to hear the rest.

00:14:52.518 --> 00:14:53.519
Anything?

00:14:56.104 --> 00:14:57.314
Thank you, sir.

00:14:57.397 --> 00:14:58.732
Now, as I was saying...

00:14:58.815 --> 00:15:00.108
Anything?

00:15:00.192 --> 00:15:03.195
Because I can give you new robotic ears.

00:15:03.278 --> 00:15:05.739
What? You can give me new ears?

00:15:05.822 --> 00:15:09.409
Wait. What seemingly reasonable thing
do you want in return?

00:15:09.493 --> 00:15:11.912
Just your hands, my dear.

00:15:11.995 --> 00:15:13.664
Whatever you said, forget it.

00:15:13.956 --> 00:15:15.999
All right, then. Just one hand.

00:15:16.542 --> 00:15:18.544
Just... my left hand?

00:15:19.419 --> 00:15:20.629
Um...

00:15:20.712 --> 00:15:22.589
Please take your seats for act two.

00:15:22.673 --> 00:15:24.508
But I'm not done vomiting.

00:15:28.095 --> 00:15:30.222
I can't stand it.

00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:32.516
Okay, you can have my hand.

00:15:32.599 --> 00:15:35.143
Wonderful! Just sign here.

00:15:36.186 --> 00:15:39.439
Calculon, old friend,
I'm afraid I need your ears.

00:15:39.523 --> 00:15:43.235
Well, I do owe you
for giving me this unholy...

00:15:43.318 --> 00:15:45.654
acting talent.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.289
I can hear. I can hear like a safecracker.

00:15:55.664 --> 00:15:57.499
Hey, aren't you gonna take my hand?

00:15:57.833 --> 00:16:00.127
In good time. You go enjoy the opera.

00:16:06.717 --> 00:16:09.803
To win Leela's heart
with the Holophonor's art

00:16:09.887 --> 00:16:13.265
I need hands of transcendental quickness

00:16:13.348 --> 00:16:15.976
Well, I don't see any danger

00:16:16.059 --> 00:16:18.520
In gambling with a stranger

00:16:18.604 --> 00:16:22.566
For my head is ofa most amazing thickness

00:16:27.696 --> 00:16:29.448
I'm stupid, I'm stupid

00:16:29.531 --> 00:16:31.366
I'm stupider than you

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:34.828
I'm stupider than you in every way

00:16:35.829 --> 00:16:37.122
Stupider?

00:16:37.206 --> 00:16:40.375
This opera is as lousy
as it is brilliant.

00:16:46.423 --> 00:16:49.218
Your lyrics lack subtlety.

00:16:49.301 --> 00:16:53.013
You can't just have your characters
announce how they feel.

00:16:53.096 --> 00:16:55.140
That makes me feel angry.

00:16:55.224 --> 00:16:56.725
Look, what do you want?

00:16:56.808 --> 00:16:58.977
I want my hands back

00:17:01.522 --> 00:17:02.940
Never.

00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.816
A deal's a deal

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.735
Even with a dirty dealer

00:17:06.818 --> 00:17:08.237
Very well, then I'll take

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:11.573
What I want from Leela

00:17:12.032 --> 00:17:13.534
Whoa.

00:17:15.244 --> 00:17:17.496
Leela has promised me her hand

00:17:18.664 --> 00:17:22.084
Fry, you do not understand!

00:17:23.335 --> 00:17:25.003
I should have revealed

00:17:25.087 --> 00:17:27.172
I'd been deafened by Bender

00:17:27.256 --> 00:17:28.841
The shame

00:17:28.924 --> 00:17:30.342
The shame!

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:32.386
But I feared you'd stop writing

00:17:32.469 --> 00:17:34.805
This musical splendor

00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:38.475
Deception's the curse
of my whimsical gender

00:17:38.559 --> 00:17:42.104
He gave me mechanical ears

00:17:42.187 --> 00:17:45.023
Effective, though just a bit garish

00:17:45.691 --> 00:17:48.318
In return, without shedding a tear

00:17:48.402 --> 00:17:51.697
I agreed that I'd give him my hand

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.407
In marriage

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.491
- Huh?
- What?

00:17:54.575 --> 00:17:58.704
You'll give me your hand in marriage

00:17:58.954 --> 00:18:00.664
Is this really happening

00:18:00.747 --> 00:18:02.332
Or just being staged?

00:18:02.416 --> 00:18:04.001
It can't be real

00:18:04.084 --> 00:18:05.669
Not if Leela is engaged

00:18:05.752 --> 00:18:07.588
That isn't what I meant

00:18:07.671 --> 00:18:09.131
That isn't what I signed

00:18:09.214 --> 00:18:11.133
You should have checked the wording

00:18:11.216 --> 00:18:13.635
In the fine...

00:18:13.719 --> 00:18:15.095
Print

00:18:15.762 --> 00:18:17.848
"I'll give you my hand..."

00:18:17.931 --> 00:18:20.058
In marriage

00:18:20.142 --> 00:18:22.853
The use of words
expressing something other

00:18:22.936 --> 00:18:25.480
Than their literal intention

00:18:25.564 --> 00:18:29.109
Now that is irony

00:18:30.819 --> 00:18:34.615
I will marry her now
and confine her to Hell

00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:36.241
How droll

00:18:36.325 --> 00:18:37.743
How droll

00:18:37.826 --> 00:18:39.703
Where Styx is a river

00:18:39.786 --> 00:18:41.580
And not just a band

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:43.498
Though they'll play our reception

00:18:43.582 --> 00:18:45.417
If all goes as planned

00:18:45.501 --> 00:18:50.380
Unless Fry, you surrender my hands!

00:18:55.511 --> 00:18:57.804
Destiny has cheated me

00:18:57.888 --> 00:19:01.433
By forcing me to decide upon

00:19:01.517 --> 00:19:03.977
The woman that I idolize

00:19:04.061 --> 00:19:06.855
Or the hands of an automaton

00:19:06.939 --> 00:19:09.608
Without these hands I can't complete

00:19:09.691 --> 00:19:11.485
The opera that was captivating her

00:19:11.568 --> 00:19:14.488
But if keep them, and she marries him

00:19:14.571 --> 00:19:19.034
Then he probably won't want me dating her

00:19:19.117 --> 00:19:20.786
Arooo.

00:19:20.869 --> 00:19:22.246
Brave-o.

00:19:22.329 --> 00:19:23.622
En-core.

00:19:23.705 --> 00:19:27.626
I can't believe
the devil is so unforgiving

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:31.839
I can't believe
everybody's just ad-libbing

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:36.260
By the power vested in me

00:19:36.343 --> 00:19:39.137
By the state of New New York...

00:19:39.221 --> 00:19:41.098
No! Stop.

00:19:41.181 --> 00:19:42.933
Take my hands...

00:19:43.016 --> 00:19:48.021
You evil... metal... dork!

00:19:54.194 --> 00:19:55.696
Surgery in an opera?

00:19:55.779 --> 00:19:57.364
How wonderfully decadent.

00:19:57.447 --> 00:20:00.325
And just as I was beginning
to lose interest.

00:20:00.409 --> 00:20:02.828
Jambi, the chocolate icing.

00:20:04.079 --> 00:20:06.832
Oh, my, yes.

00:20:06.915 --> 00:20:09.126
Ooh.

00:20:09.209 --> 00:20:11.295
My hands.

00:20:11.378 --> 00:20:13.922
My horrible human hands.

00:20:14.006 --> 00:20:16.383
And what did you do to my nails?

00:20:16.466 --> 00:20:18.010
I cleaned them.

00:20:18.093 --> 00:20:20.262
Now, if you'll excuse me,
it's my poker night

00:20:20.345 --> 00:20:22.264
and I feel lucky.

00:20:22.681 --> 00:20:24.725
So, it's back to Hell for me.

00:20:24.808 --> 00:20:26.435
- Come on, Nixon.
- Huh?

00:20:30.856 --> 00:20:33.734
Less reality, more fantasy.

00:20:33.817 --> 00:20:35.527
Resume the opera.

00:20:35.611 --> 00:20:37.529
But I can't play anymore.

00:20:37.613 --> 00:20:38.947
Yes, you can.

00:20:39.031 --> 00:20:40.657
The beauty was in your heart,

00:20:40.741 --> 00:20:41.909
not your hands.

00:20:54.296 --> 00:20:56.924
Your music's bad, and you should feel bad.

00:20:59.843 --> 00:21:01.512
Whoa.

00:21:02.012 --> 00:21:03.013
Hey.

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:06.433
Extra, extra.

00:21:06.517 --> 00:21:08.977
Greatest opera of all time sucks.

00:21:09.061 --> 00:21:10.270
I'll take eight.

00:21:20.864 --> 00:21:22.824
Please don't stop playing, Fry.

00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:25.994
I want to hear how it ends.